  "_readme": [
    "Rooted genre taxonomy for the 'taxonomy' (Lin) similarity method and the",
    "hybrid retrofit. A DAG, not a strict tree: derived genres may name two",
    "parents (tech house descends from both house and techno). Keys are",
    "normalized labels (lowercase, hyphens as spaces, '&' spelled); values are",
    "parent label arrays. Everything reaches the root 'music'. Modelled on",
    "Wikipedia stylistic-origin infoboxes and musicmap.info lineage; edit",
    "freely — similarity is Lin's measure over intrinsic information content,",
    "so genres with a deep, specific common ancestor score high while pairs",
    "relating only through umbrella nodes (electronic, pop) score low."
  ],
